{"source":{"data":"@method=GET @endpoint=ews/collections/alerts\nFeature: Fetch alerts (API.EWS.03, OGC API Features)\n\nAPI.EWS.03 Fetch Alert exposes the EWS alerts as an OGC API Features collection:\nGET /collections/alerts, GET /collections/alerts/items, filtered on CAP properties\n(?event=Flood, ?severity=Extreme, ?urgency=Immediate, ...), and one alert by identifier.\nEvery alert returned is a DO.EWS.01 Alert (GeoJSON Feature) carrying a valid CapAlert.\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # The collection\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: The alerts collection is described\n    Given the \"alerts collection\" endpoint\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid \"collection\"\n    And the collection should link to its items\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Items\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: The alerts are returned as a FeatureCollection of valid alerts\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have the content type \"application/geo+json\"\n    And the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\"\n    And at least 1 alert should be returned\n    And numberReturned should match the features returned\n    And every alert in the collection should be a different alert\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: Alerts filtered by <property> = <value> all match the filter\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    And the alerts are filtered by \"<property>\" = \"<value>\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\"\n    And every returned alert should have \"<property>\" = \"<value>\"\n    And numberReturned should match the features returned\n\n    Examples: Filters of API.EWS.03\n      | property | value     |\n      | event    | Flood     |\n      | severity | Extreme   |\n      | urgency  | Immediate |\n\n    Examples: Other CAP properties\n      | property         | value                |\n      | certainty        | Observed             |\n      | category         | Met                  |\n      | category         | MET                  |\n      | status           | Actual               |\n      | status           | Exercise             |\n      | msg_type         | Update               |\n      | scope            | Public               |\n      | threshold_status | TRIGGER              |\n      | event_code       | DR                   |\n\n  @functional @mock\n  Scenario Outline: The mock collection holds alerts for <property> = <value>\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    And the alerts are filtered by \"<property>\" = \"<value>\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\"\n    And at least <count> alerts should be returned\n\n    Examples:\n      | property  | value       | count |\n      | severity  | Extreme     | 2     |\n      | category  | Met         | 3     |\n      | event     | Flash Flood | 1     |\n      | status    | Exercise    | 1     |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: A filter value nobody matches returns an empty FeatureCollection\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    And the alerts are filtered by \"urgency\" = \"Unknown\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\"\n    And no alert should be returned\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: limit caps the number of alerts returned\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    And at most 2 alerts are asked for\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\"\n    And at most 2 alerts should be returned\n    And numberReturned should match the features returned\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid filter is rejected: <property> = <value>\n    Given the \"alert items\" endpoint\n    And the query parameter \"<property>\" is \"<value>\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be an OGC exception with HTTP status 400\n\n    Examples:\n      | property         | value        |\n      | severity         | Catastrophic |\n      | severity         | extreme      |\n      | urgency          | Now          |\n      | certainty        | Sure         |\n      | category         | Weather      |\n      | status           | Real         |\n      | threshold_status | RED          |\n      | limit            | 0            |\n      | limit            | many         |\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # One alert\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: One alert is returned by its identifier\n    Given the \"alert item\" endpoint\n    And the alert \"existing\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be a valid \"alert\"\n\n  @functional @mock\n  Scenario Outline: The <alert> alert is returned by its identifier\n    Given the \"alert item\" endpoint\n    And the alert \"<alert>\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"alert\"\n    And the returned alert should be \"<alert>\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | alert        |\n      | spec example |\n      | full         |\n      | earthquake   |\n      | heatwave     |\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: An unknown alert is not found\n    Given the \"alert item\" endpoint\n    And the alert \"unknown\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be an OGC exception with HTTP status 404\n","uri":"features/ews_alerts_collection.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=GET","id":"049db74e-fce0-460c-8e26-afe39d52e673"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":13},"name":"@endpoint=ews/collections/alerts","id":"8db61ea4-1946-461f-adb7-ace080bc0290"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Fetch alerts (API.EWS.03, OGC API Features)","description":"API.EWS.03 Fetch Alert exposes the EWS alerts as an OGC API Features collection:\nGET /collections/alerts, GET /collections/alerts/items, filtered on CAP properties\n(?event=Flood, ?severity=Extreme, ?urgency=Immediate, ...), and one alert by identifier.\nEvery alert returned is a DO.EWS.01 Alert (GeoJSON Feature) carrying a valid CapAlert.","children":[{"scenario":{"id":"a51067e2-af79-4a35-ac90-4c2d1c77a3b3","tags":[{"location":{"line":12,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"f60990ee-3921-4a4b-8d9d-eb721d8392c6"}],"location":{"line":13,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"The alerts collection is described","description":"","steps":[{"id":"43d6ac6b-4881-4d97-b43c-7ecafd71903d","location":{"line":14,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"alerts collection\" endpoint"},{"id":"4cac9ec3-1fa7-4c2b-9a77-e1776af9974f","location":{"line":15,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"d743942d-49fc-45dd-8347-d2026b968ab8","location":{"line":16,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"8a634b68-60a6-4f14-9559-a4493bfd106a","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"62a22a4f-2ff5-4c2a-977d-36bd5eba7713","location":{"line":18,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"3d733045-2561-4950-ade6-63d16313fa39","location":{"line":19,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid \"collection\""},{"id":"351944c8-592d-4150-8413-87b85feeb79c","location":{"line":20,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the collection should link to its items"}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"e7debf2a-d7c9-49cf-910d-7eec78005427","tags":[{"location":{"line":25,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"e6931900-7db3-4257-8f74-8a90beac8ce9"}],"location":{"line":26,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"The alerts are returned as a FeatureCollection of valid alerts","description":"","steps":[{"id":"bd1c7e78-b7f8-42d3-82f6-6b26deebb033","location":{"line":27,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"alert items\" endpoint"},{"id":"efdbb7eb-5e91-41d8-b550-b673b987719d","location":{"line":28,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"bbffa59b-c440-4d5e-8965-52e6a2029407","location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"d03c81bb-6770-4add-85e2-43e3fed7d016","location":{"line":30,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have the content type \"application/geo+json\""},{"id":"3aff38c0-bd69-428b-881a-415544b3de47","location":{"line":31,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\""},{"id":"b2940a95-40ef-4664-a6f5-1ebe058812fd","location":{"line":32,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"at least 1 alert should be returned"},{"id":"686ff3ae-765f-4eca-809d-2f3ec1bedf64","location":{"line":33,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"numberReturned should match the features returned"},{"id":"3ed3c45d-f171-4630-b081-e91ee4302add","location":{"line":34,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"every alert in the collection should be a different alert"}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"8aa1ed55-a1b8-4618-a1d8-4da298effd0e","tags":[{"location":{"line":36,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"d0d2192a-242c-4e36-b3a5-bb0080cdd329"}],"location":{"line":37,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"Alerts filtered by <property> = <value> all match the filter","description":"","steps":[{"id":"192ed70d-5726-48a3-a962-9e36da773fbb","location":{"line":38,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"alert items\" endpoint"},{"id":"8b28107a-24fd-45d7-8bb8-d51468e3d7d5","location":{"line":39,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the alerts are filtered by \"<property>\" = \"<value>\""},{"id":"e6421340-f3c1-4eaa-9bcc-e3581ed29fa3","location":{"line":40,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"70247783-44e0-4901-bbb1-3625aae07de0","location":{"line":41,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the response should be a valid \"feature-collection\""},{"id":"f8d80ef0-c305-40fa-bbdc-049a5a58bf8e","location":{"line":42,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"every returned alert should have \"<property>\" = \"<value>\""},{"id":"4236a68d-07de-459d-8f01-37aea1e906db","location":{"line":43,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"numberReturned should match the features returned"}],"examples":[{"id":"937a0427-2afc-4906-86d3-880d5c00923b","tags":[],"location":{"line":45,"column":5},"keyword":"Examples","name":"Filters of API.EWS.03","description":"","tableHeader":{"id":"47a82ac3-d589-4cdd-9eb0-019557c5c2eb","location":{"line":46,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":46,"column":9},"value":"property"},{"location":{"line":46,"column":20},"value":"value"}]},"tableBody":[{"id":"3dd91900-19d9-4514-8ca8-3435a1de4256","location":{"line":47,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":47,"column":9},"value":"event"},{"location":{"line":47,"column":20},"value":"Flood"}]},{"id":"952d0a03-b093-44e1-