{"pickle":{"id":"d6fed31f-4f1b-4f53-807b-3ef6a451a568","uri":"features/ews_sdmx_data.feature","astNodeIds":["df820cea-19be-4e79-a11a-9061a3eecb8e","5d57cf10-b760-444b-87ea-fafb30b81b7a"],"name":"DCI statistics with a count below the minimum are rejected","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"d9244077-b1d6-4f4d-8bd1-fe6318470f22","text":"the \"spec example\" DciStatistics record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["cf1daca9-150f-4f2a-ad25-27d05a1a1a1f","5d57cf10-b760-444b-87ea-fafb30b81b7a"]},{"id":"e54a849b-7657-4e34-85c8-a18021a7a77e","text":"its \"data.dataSets.0.observations\" attribute is set to '{\"AREA001.F.TRUE.ALL.IPC_3_PLUS\":{\"OBS_VALUE\":2}}'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["5d757557-80ac-44b1-a391-f1a41bb17312","5d57cf10-b760-444b-87ea-fafb30b81b7a"]},{"id":"079023b0-e8a8-4f3b-9704-037336620137","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"below the minimum cell count\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["fd27d3ec-a302-4d8d-aaa4-9af6da0ae3b6","5d57cf10-b760-444b-87ea-fafb30b81b7a"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"721779c7-6c92-4783-afda-df48788d7cd4"}]}}
{"pickle":{"id":"6ea115d3-da31-42ac-b272-d365c336c419","uri":"features/ews_sdmx_data.feature","astNodeIds":["df820cea-19be-4e79-a11a-9061a3eecb8e","a16e811f-75fc-4eed-ba9d-8077495b6182"],"name":"DCI statistics with an unknown dataset attribute are rejected","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"99142959-6ceb-4fe9-86ab-f364f1fbc2dc","text":"the \"spec example\" DciStatistics record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["cf1daca9-150f-4f2a-ad25-27d05a1a1a1f","a16e811f-75fc-4eed-ba9d-8077495b6182"]},{"id":"c1eed6a9-412b-4441-b879-a4634aa28f9b","text":"its \"data.dataSets.0.attributes.BENEFICIARY_NAMES\" attribute is set to '\"...\"'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["5d757557-80ac-44b1-a391-f1a41bb17312","a16e811f-75fc-4eed-ba9d-8077495b6182"]},{"id":"808ff026-2556-4674-ab4d-c8620700c89b","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"dataset attribute \"BENEFICIARY_NAMES\" is not defined\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["fd27d3ec-a302-4d8d-aaa4-9af6da0ae3b6","a16e811f-75fc-4eed-ba9d-8077495b6182"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"721779c7-6c92-4783-afda-df48788d7cd4"}]}}
{"pickle":{"id":"fdde8de2-18e7-4501-840a-324b8de3a853","uri":"features/ews_sdmx_data.feature","astNodeIds":["f969fa4b-7d45-4865-989f-4f9ff24f3407"],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"721779c7-6c92-4783-afda-df48788d7cd4"}],"name":"Both published key layouts are accepted (… TIME_PERIOD and … DENOMINATOR_TYPE)","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"96c0d604-25cb-4266-98f4-4812fbe0707f","text":"the \"spec example\" DciStatistics record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["9d784932-231c-4a07-ad8e-04d30f2d1df0"]},{"id":"10e2b446-9ea8-416f-be4d-e957ab87293b","text":"its \"data.dataSets.0.observations\" attribute is set to '{\"AREA001.F.TRUE.ALL.IPC_3_PLUS\":{\"OBS_VALUE\":1250},\"AREA001.F.TRUE.ALL.2026\":{\"OBS_VALUE\":3421}}'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["b2a84237-522d-4115-a4a1-a7734040c941"]},{"id":"5985a3e1-95a3-4de7-bf80-dfbe0702e0e7","text":"the record should be valid","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["1eed56ea-5ddf-408c-989a-09ce2c3655cf"]}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ews/subscribe\nFeature: Subscribe to early warning alerts (API.EWS.01, POST /subscribe)\n\nAPI.EWS.01 Event Subscription: \"An SP system can subscribe to receive alerts and define what\ntype of events and severity.\" The SP system names the alerts it wants (filter: event, event\ncode, category, severity, urgency, certainty, threshold status, status, message type, area)\nand how they are delivered (notify_record_type: CapAlert or Alert). The EWS acknowledges the\nrequest and delivers the subscription result to the on-subscribe callback.\n\nThe standard publishes no envelope for this API: the suite uses the DCI message envelope\nshared by every DCI API, with the EWS alert filter in subscribe_criteria.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"subscribe\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: A subscription to severe and extreme floods is acknowledged\n    Given a subscribe request for \"floods of severe or extreme severity\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: A subscription to <filter>, notified as <type> records, is acknowledged\n    Given a subscribe request for \"<filter>\" notified as <type> records\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n    Examples: Event types and severity (API.EWS.01)\n      | filter                                 | type     |\n      | floods of severe or extreme severity   | CapAlert |\n      | droughts by event code                 | CapAlert |\n      | immediate alerts                       | Alert    |\n      | alerts crossing a threshold            | Alert    |\n\n    Examples: Categories, as values and as CD.EWS.01 codes\n      | filter                                 | type     |\n      | meteorological alerts                  | CapAlert |\n      | meteorological alerts by category code | CapAlert |\n\n    Examples: Areas and message types\n      | filter                                 | type     |\n      | alerts for an administrative area      | Alert    |\n      | alerts for a polygon                   | Alert    |\n      | actual alerts only                     | CapAlert |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: A batch subscription with several filters is acknowledged\n    Given a batch subscribe request for \"floods of severe or extreme severity; droughts by event code; alerts for an administrative area\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Full async round trip\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @callback\n  Scenario Outline: The subscription result for <filter> is delivered to the on-subscribe callback\n    Given a subscribe request for \"<filter>\" notified as <type> records\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-subscribe\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-subscribe\" message\n    And every subscription should be confirmed with a subscription code\n    And every subscription should echo the requested filter and record type\n\n    Examples:\n      | filter                               | type     |\n      | floods of severe or extreme severity | CapAlert |\n      | alerts for an administrative area    | Alert    |\n\n  @callback\n  Scenario: Every item of a batch subscription is confirmed in the callback\n    Given a batch subscribe request for \"immediate alerts; alerts crossing a threshold\"\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-subscribe\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-subscribe\" message\n    And every subscription should be confirmed with a subscription code\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Invalid requests\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid subscription is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples: Envelope\n      | case                     | field                                                  | value                  |\n      | missing header           | header                                                 | <removed>              |\n      | wrong action             | header.action                                          | \"notify\"               |\n      | missing sender_id        | header.sender_id                                       | <removed>              |\n      | missing message          | message                                                | <removed>              |\n      | missing transaction_id   | message.transaction_id                                 | <removed>              |\n      | empty subscribe_request  | message.subscribe_request                              | []                     |\n      | missing reference_id     | message.subscribe_request.0.reference_id               | <removed>              |\n      | missing criteria         | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria         | <removed>              |\n      | invalid locale           | message.subscribe_request.0.locale                     | \"en-GB\"                |\n\n    Examples: Alert filter (API.EWS.01: what type of events and severity)\n      | case                          | field                                                                 | value                    |\n      | missing filter                | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter                 | <removed>                |\n      | empty filter                  | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter                 | {}                       |\n      | severity outside CD.EWS.02    | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.severity        | [\"High\"]                 |\n      | severity as a single value    | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.severity        | \"Severe\"                 |\n      | empty severity list           | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.severity        | []                       |\n      | category outside CD.EWS.01    | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.category        | [\"Weather\"]              |\n      | urgency outside CD.EWS.06     | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.urgency         | [\"Now\"]                  |\n      | certainty outside CD.EWS.07   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.certainty       | [\"Certain\"]              |\n      | threshold outside CD.EWS.10   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.threshold_status | [\"RED\"]                 |\n      | status outside CD.EWS.03      | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.status          | [\"Real\"]                 |\n      | event code outside CD.EWS.01  | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.event_code      | [\"XX\"]                   |\n      | area without description      | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.area            | [{}]                     |\n      | area polygon not lat,lon      | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter.area            | [{\"polygon\":[\"33.85 35.45\"]}] |\n      | missing notify_record_type    | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.notify_record_type     | <removed>                |\n      | unknown notify_record_type    | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.notify_record_type     | \"Person\"                 |\n      | incomplete frequency          | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.frequency              | {\"frequency\":\"daily\"}    |\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: A body that is not JSON is rejected\n    When the raw body \"not json\" is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n","uri":"features/ews_subscribe.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"bbf20c7f-7aa2-412b-9447-3296183c7dbc"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ews/subscribe","id":"6b46cf0a-2c0d-427d-bb6b-97b7e49e1458"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Subscribe to early warning alerts (API.EWS.01, POST /subscribe)","description":"API.EWS.01 Event Subscription: \"An SP system can subscribe to receive alerts and define what\ntype of events and severity.\" The SP system names the alerts it wants (filter: event, event\ncode, category, severity, urgency, certainty, threshold status, status, message type, area)\nand how they are delivered (notify_record_type: CapAlert or Alert). The EWS acknowledges the\nrequest and delivers the subscription result to the on-subscribe callback.\n\nThe standard publishes no envelope for this API: the suite uses the DCI message envelope\nshared by every DCI API, with the EWS alert filter in subscribe_criteria.","children":[{"background":{"id":"79ecd765-4403-45ab-86aa-a80e5811ca0f","location":{"line":13,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"205c0756-e479-4ebe-b7a5-0f5c95ade016","location":{"line":14,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"subscribe\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"58585aa6-68a7-4119-82f7-a1df126f8360","tags":[{"location":{"line":16,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"b36d226f-5072-4bc4-b321-9ef2c6fdf99e"}],"location":{"line":17,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"A subscription to severe and extreme floods is acknowledged","description":"","steps":[{"id":"4957eb72-d43b-49ac-9814-64486bbf9a0a","location":{"line":18,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a subscribe request for \"floods of severe or extreme severity\""},{"id":"04346354-3828-4300-abc5-d82c4a454763","location":{"line":19,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message"},{"id":"bd58382e-ccdb-4c44-aabb-e6d182549d29","location":{"line":20,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"565554c4-75c3-468a-acc4-7ac7012d561a","location":{"line":21,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"4a48d99c-16cf-4378-a623-fab666382101","location":{"line":22,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"20fbd81b-1642-45d0-8a7f-14b7c476d1e4","location":{"line":23,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"3bec6524-4462-4174-9e50-1faafbc52948","location":{"line":24,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\""}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"03b01c11-9313-438b-8a25-2f7d0ee708bc","tags":[{"location":{"line":26,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"5af602a7-f6fb-4263-a029-6f4d57f4861a"}],"location":{"line":27,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"A subscription to <filter>, notified as <type> records, is acknowledged","description":"","steps":[{"id":"1c955d0a-dee4-4f54-b41c-ded551efe3fa","location":{"line":28,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a subscribe request for \"<filter>\" notified as <type> records"},{"id":"f3cb3843-b917-4a35-8825-b53f9b56fb91","location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message"},{"id":"d1e65970-85c7-4848-84a6-c7322e22c225","location":{"line":30,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"0203bc2b-d51a-4272-ad1e-d3cfe2e1c83f","location":{"line":31,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status 